From 64c02b14eee6ca155ffde375f348715ab8f34224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:02:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): quota-episode routing checks walls it didn't
 record, falls back to the strong tier, and feeds its deadline to the stuck
 warning [daveey]

Follow-ups from the Opus review of PR #578 (t_01a19987de068d42):
- decision() used to admit a target provider just because this episode had not hit it. A target that
  provider_walls.json or the live OAuth pool shows as walled now counts as walled. This also holds
  explicit pins and review-lane cards whose provider is walled elsewhere; they wait and the pin is not
  rewritten. Once the episode is over, resolve_dispatch_tier applies the provider-wall reroute again
  (it gated on episode() before, now on active()). So a card that moved off codex and was then walled
  on anthropic is not routed back to walled codex during the episode or after it.
- When no class alternate exists, an unpinned default episode card now takes main's strong-tier
  retier_for_walls fallback. That covers routing off, a default model in no class or in more than one,
  and a class whose routes are all walled. The fallback is judged against the episode's own walls too
  (new extra_walls). Explicit pins still wait for the reset.
- guard_hold_until() reads the episode's outstanding deadline (doubling backoff, every provider's wall)
  for subscription_quota_reset and rate_limit_cooldown. The stuck warning's "(until ...)" now matches
  the guard instead of ended_at + one cooldown.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_quota_episode_walls.py. 11 fail on main and 13/13 pass here (the
other 2 are controls). In test_new_unpinned_card_created_after_a_known_wall_never_routes_to_it, the
first card is now archived to isolate the tick: its own episode now reroutes it, which is the fixed
behaviour, and a raw status='blocked' did not keep it out of the tick.
